Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: an analytic blend whose contact passes over a hole of its face is
cut by the hole's wall also where the wall's seam runs up from its rim
under the blend: the cut is made in two pieces, one on each side of the
seam, and the seam is cut where the blend crosses it (mitcad#2365, GitHub
mitcad/Mitcad#635).

The case: a block's end edges along a chamfered bottom rounded with 2,
with a counterbore 15 wide through the chamfer whose rim comes 1 mm from
each end face. The contact on the chamfer passes over the counterbore.
Where the counterbore's seam lies away from the rounding (at one end), the
gap is filled as patch 0055 fills it: the blend runs on over the hole and
the counterbore's wall cuts it. At the other end, the same counterbore
turned the other way, its seam runs up from the rim under the blend, and
ChFi3d_KPartCutPiece refuses a piece with a vertex of the face beyond
under the blend (0055: B would have to grow along that edge up to the
cut). The gap was left to the walking, which rounded the wall's top
from the end face over to the counterbore's wall: 1.22 mm3 more material
than the mirror image at the other end, the end face's edge with the
rounding bent down beside the hole, two more faces. Rounded together, the
two ends differed the same way.

- ChFi3d_KPartCutChainFrom: in a chain round from the face beyond back to
  it (Round, ChFi3d_FillKPartGaps' last resort for a gap whose two ends lie
  on one face beyond), the face's own seam leads back to the face: the
  chain is that face twice, the seam the edge crossed between them. The
  crossing is found as for any edge (ChFi3d_KPartEdgeCrossing), and the
  seam, in the chain's cut edges, no longer refuses the pieces' vertex
  check.
- ChFi3d_KPartChainPieces: a crossing on a seam of a chain of one face
  twice is taken, for the piece before it, on the side of the seam (its
  p-curve and its orientation in the face) nearest the piece's start on
  the face (Prev's arc), for the piece after it on the side nearest that
  piece's end (Next's arc); its transition on the seam is the one of the
  piece before.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 2365.
